markdown <<MARKDOWN
# What Counts as a Pedestrian?

Two classification models have been trained to spot pedestrians, people walking, in street photos. Below, toggle between Model 1 and Model 2 to see how each one classifies the exact same eight photos, then make your own call on which model you'd actually use.

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-2/pedestrian-model-compare.html"
    width="100%"
    height="1050"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Compare Model 1 and Model 2 pedestrian classifications across eight photos, then choose and reveal which model you'd use">
  </iframe>
</div>



<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Teacher tip:</b> students will default to calling Model 1 the better model because it's more accurate. Don't correct that yet, let them sit with it, then ask the next question: if these models decide when a self-driving car stops, which one do you want behind the wheel?</div>
</div>

Now reframe the question. These models decide when a self-driving car stops, it stops for a pedestrian and keeps going otherwise. Suddenly Model 2's mistakes look less like errors and more like caution. It treats a motorcycle, a bicycle, and a car near a crosswalk the same way it treats a person on foot: worth stopping for. That's the choice built into the activity above, click one and the real reasoning reveals underneath it.

<div style="background-color: #FFE3CE; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#9888;&#65039; Watch for:</b> students who treat "classify more things as pedestrians" as a free win. Push them further, a model that calls everything a pedestrian is also safe by this definition, but useless. The real skill here is picking a category, and a threshold, that matches what the model is actually for.</div>
</div>
MARKDOWN
